      "content": "That works. Now, looking at both, I noticed the tone is quite different. The Oakwood Heights one feels very \"safe\" and \"exclusive,\" while the East District one feels more \"active\" and \"unpredictable.\"\n\nCan you explain why you chose those specific descriptors for each? Like, why did you go with words like \"legacy\" and \"refined\" for one, but \"raw\" and \"bustling\" for the other? I'm curious about the logic behind how you differentiate these types of neighborhoods for a luxury audience.",
